      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their problem was that Event Nexus search relevance degraded, with saved searches returning poor and duplicate results, increasing manual triage time to about 6 hours per day. The proof plan proposed to get them comfortable with renewal involved a short-term fix to update index weighting and add a mapping layer translating new taxonomy terms to historical query tokens for the top 20 saved searches. This included receiving schema registry exports and query logs by 2026-03-19, starting an A/B test in staging on 2026-03-22 lasting 7-10 business days, and validating that the top-5 correct hit rate would be at least 80% for prioritized queries. If successful, a 1-day production rollout and 72-hour monitoring would follow. Additionally, a 90-day fixed-price professional services engagement for $48k was offered to implement the tuning and mapping, with a 30% discount if Orchestrator expansion was signed concurrently. A conditional credit on renewal was also proposed if the proof did not meet the agreed accuracy uplift within 10 business days. This plan was designed to demonstrate measurable improvement within the executive mandate timeframe and reduce manual triage burden, thereby supporting renewal confidence [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_bd3560dfe194, art_0bccc580184e].",
