      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were the \"department\" and \"businessUnit\" attributes, which were inconsistently used across teams\u2014Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant while Payments Ops used department=payments. This inconsistency caused ingestion normalization failures and routing mismatches in the Rules Engine. Jin proposed a fast fix by adding a preprocessing mapping rule in Signal Ingest to map businessUnit to department (or vice versa) to produce a normalized canonical attribute for correlation. This fix is a configuration-only, hot-reloadable change that does not require Okta change control or appliance restarts, enabling a quick resolution without waiting for Okta change control approval [art_79f625aafa16, art_e60697c15fce].",
